---
import MarketingLayout from '@/layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@sections/content/PageHeader.astro';
import StatsSection from '@sections/social-proof/StatsSection.astro';
import ValuesSection from '@sections/team/ValuesSection.astro';
import ContentSection from '@sections/content/ContentSection.astro';
import CTA from '@sections/marketing/CTA.astro';
import { siteConfig, company } from '@/config';

const values = [
  {
    title: 'Structured, not marketing copy',
    description:
      'Every vehicle is a normalized product record — battery chemistry, powertrain architecture, dimensions, versions, and technology — with provenance attached, not a promotional blurb.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Provenance over assertion',
    description:
      'Each figure carries a source type and an update date, and any field we could not verify is marked as not recorded rather than filled with a guess.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Product-first',
    description:
      'Built for anyone researching Chinese EVs — buyers, analysts, journalists, and enthusiasts — who needs a structured record rather than sales copy.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Honest about limits',
    description:
      'We state plainly what this platform is and is not: an information platform, not a seller, importer, or broker. See the full policy pages for the fine print.',
  },
];

import { getSiteStats } from '@/lib/site-stats';
const s = await getSiteStats();
const stats = [
  { value: String(s.vehicles), label: 'Vehicles cataloged' },
  { value: String(s.brands), label: 'Chinese brands' },
  { value: String(s.bevCount + s.phevCount + s.erevCount + s.hevCount + s.iceCount), label: 'Powertrains indexed' },
  { value: '4', label: 'Range test standards tracked' },
];
---

<MarketingLayout
  title={`About - ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description="What China EV Mart is and is not: an independent information platform for discovering Chinese new-energy vehicles — not a seller, importer, or broker."
>
  <PageHeader title="An independent platform for Chinese EV data" align="left" maxWidth="lg">
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
      Chinese EV specifications are scattered across manufacturer sites, press releases, and
      forum posts, in inconsistent formats and with no source provenance. Most research starts
      by piecing together spec sheets from several places — and still ends up with gaps.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
      {siteConfig.name} exists to make that data structured and checkable <em>before</em> you rely
      on it. Every vehicle page is a normalized product record — battery chemistry, powertrain,
      dimensions, versions, and technology — with the source and update date attached to each
      figure.
    </p>
  </PageHeader>

  <StatsSection stats={stats} background="muted" />

  <ValuesSection
    title="What we stand for"
    items={values}
    variant="card"
    columns={2}
    background="default"
  />

  <ContentSection
    title="What this platform does"
    content={[
      `${siteConfig.name} catalogs Chinese new-energy vehicle records — specifications, versions, battery and powertrain data, and export-relevant facts such as HS code classification. It is operated by ${company.name} (${company.legalName}) and edited by ${company.author}, ${company.authorRole}.`,
      "Our specification methodology is published in full, so any reader can judge how a figure was sourced. We record battery chemistry and architecture at the vehicle level, apply a consistent normalization scheme, and mark any field we could not verify as not recorded rather than guessing.",
      "We publish the data model, the source types, and the range and price conventions on the methodology and data-provenance pages, so the record is auditable rather than a black box.",
    ]}
    background="default"
  />

  <ContentSection
    title="What this platform does not do"
    content={[
      `${siteConfig.name} does not sell vehicles and is not a dealer, importer, customs broker, or purchasing agent. It is not affiliated with any manufacturer, and its inclusion of a brand or model does not imply endorsement.`,
      "We do not provide quotes, transactional prices, live inventory, or sourcing/matchmaking. Where a reader asks about a specific model, we can offer specification guidance only — see the FAQ.",
      "We do not run battery, range, or safety tests, and we do not present any figure as a measured result when it is not. Where independent test data is cited, it is attributed to whoever ran the test.",
      "We do not claim credentials, awards, testing facilities, partnerships, or client relationships we do not have. Any credential we state is one we can point to.",
    ]}
    background="muted"
  />

  <ContentSection
    title="About the author & review process"
    content={[
      `${company.author} is ${siteConfig.name}'s ${company.authorRole}. He spent many years in automotive battery production before turning to product research on electric vehicles — battery chemistry, powertrain architecture, and cross-border compliance.`,
      "Records are compiled from public sources — manufacturer datasheets, type-approval databases, and industry records — and stamped with an update date and verification status so readers can judge freshness. Where a record has not yet been human-reviewed, that status is shown rather than implied away.",
    ]}
    background="default"
  />

  <ContentSection
    title="Operating entity & editorial responsibility"
    content={[
      `${siteConfig.name} is operated by ${company.name} (${company.legalName}), which also maintains the vehicle database. Editorial analysis is written and reviewed by ${company.author}, ${company.authorRole}, who is the named author on trade and tariff articles.`,
      "Where a figure or a cost statement is an estimate rather than a recorded or measured value, it is labelled as such. Landed-cost figures are published on the electricvehiclehub.net sister site, whose methodology is referenced rather than reproduced here.",
      `${siteConfig.name} is an independent information platform. Its data records and editorial analysis do not represent the official position of any vehicle manufacturer, brand, or government authority. Manufacturer specifications are attributed to the manufacturer, not stated as this platform's own findings.`,
    ]}
    background="muted"
  />

  <ContentSection
    title="Operator disclosure & relationship to Chengguang Energy"
    content={[
      `This platform's own records identify its operator as ${company.name} (${company.legalName}), founded 2002, described as an automotive battery manufacturer whose quality management system is certified to IATF 16949. The records name ${company.author} (${company.authorRole}) as editor.`,
      `The operator–author relationship is recorded as an employment relationship, but this site's entity data marks it "NEEDS_REVIEW" — meaning the exact nature of the relationship between ${company.name} and ${company.author} (employee, contractor, or otherwise) has not been confirmed against a primary document. We disclose this openly rather than asserting a precise employment status we cannot point to.`,
      "Pending operator confirmation, the following items remain open and are listed for manual completion:",
    ]}
    background="default"
  />

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-6 -mt-4">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 px-5 py-4">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-2">Operator disclosure — pending manual confirmation</p>
      <ul class="text-sm text-amber-700 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li>Confirm the exact nature of the relationship between Chengguang Energy and Wei Wang (employee / contractor / principal).</li>
        <li>Provide a primary source for the IATF 16949 certification claim (certificate number or registry reference).</li>
        <li>Confirm the legal relationship between China EV Mart (platform) and Chengguang Energy (operator), and between China EV Mart and the electricvehiclehub.net sister site.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <CTA
    title="Start with the structured record"
    description="Browse the catalog and see the sourced, dated specification for any Chinese EV."
    action={{ label: 'Explore Vehicles', href: '/vehicles' }}
    background="muted"
  />
</MarketingLayout>
